{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-26T22:07:45.899Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n**Summary of what I did:**\n\n1. **Added `src/core/trace/lookup-root.ts`** — moved the openspec-root ancestor search (`findOpenspecRoot`) out of `scenario-lookup.ts`, and added the linked-worktree branch read: it reads `<root>/.git`, resolves the `gitdir:` line against the folder, reads the linked `HEAD`, and accepts a change folder only when `HEAD` reads `ref: refs/heads/osq/<folder>` and `<openspecRoot>/changes/<folder>` is a directory. Results are cached per openspec root, with `clearLookupRootCache` to drop them. Only `node:fs`/`node:path` are imported.\n\n2. **Changed `src/core/trace/scenario-lookup.ts`** — imports the new module; without `OSQ_CHANGE`, `resolveLocation` now uses `worktreeChangeFolder(openspecRoot)`; `clearScenarioLookupCache` also clears the worktree cache. Down from 247 to 239 lines.\n\n3. **Added `tests/trace-worktree-change.test.ts`** — five tests through `lookupScenario`, building trees in temp dirs with hand-written `.git`/`HEAD` files and no git, covering \"Change from the worktree branch\", \"Worktree change already archived\", \"Checkout or other branch\" (directory and non-`osq/`), and \"Branch read once\".\n\nVerification: the task's `verify` passes (5/5), the existing traceability tests pass, budgets pass, and the full `pnpm verify` (typecheck CLI/UI, build, all tests, lint) passes. Result written to `openspec/changes/095-osq-message-and-leftovers/.run/results/1.md`."}}
